{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And anoint yourself</b>. Oil that has a good fragrance, for such is the custom of the great ones of Israel, men and women." "<b>And put your garments upon you</b> — the good ones in which she was not gleaning." "<b>His feet</b>. Like רגליו, and so in Daniel. Therefore the commentator erred, for it is a cushion placed under the feet, like the sense of מראשותיו, which is placed under the head."], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:37.891123175Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}